Third-party material
====================

Included in this repository
---------------------------

1. cl100k_base tokenizer vocabulary
   File: synap/cloud/shared/data/cl100k_base.tiktoken
   What it is: OpenAI's cl100k_base byte-pair vocabulary, in the format of the tiktoken
   library, used to count tokens when the library cannot download it. The server checks
   the file against a fixed SHA-256 before it uses it.
   Source: https://github.com/openai/tiktoken (MIT License, Copyright (c) 2022 OpenAI,
   Shantanu Jain). The vocabulary is published by OpenAI for use with tiktoken.

2. LongMemEval questions and answers
   File: benchmarks/results/longmemeval/question_records.json
   What it is: the 500 questions and reference answers of LongMemEval (Wu et al.,
   ICLR 2025, https://arxiv.org/abs/2410.10813), with this project's retrieved memories
   and results, and quoted excerpts of the conversation sessions the questions refer to.
   Source: https://github.com/xiaowu0162/LongMemEval and
   https://huggingface.co/datasets/xiaowu0162/longmemeval-cleaned, both under the MIT
   License. The dataset's filler sessions come from ShareGPT and UltraChat, as its authors
   describe; excerpts of them keep whatever terms those sources carry.

